# Binary assets must never go through line-ending normalization.
#
# Committing a PDF produced "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time
# Git touches it". The stored blob was fine, but a fresh clone on Windows
# would have had CR bytes injected into the PDF stream -- a file that is
# correct in this working copy and corrupt for whoever clones it next,
# which is the worst version of this bug because it is invisible here.
*.pdf   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
